## Priority 2 — Establish the core Operator I theorem hierarchy

### Objective

Give rigorous content to controlled, robust, epistemic, and institutional viability, actual-state membership, recoverability, obstruction certificates, and quantitative margins.

### Why second

Operator I is the mathematical engine common to ecological, economic, social, and governance applications.

### Required work

- verify robust tangency/strong-invariance assumptions;
- organize the abstract-to-restricted information-kernel ladder;
- integrate emergency-envelope and informational recovery;
- verify sampled, tube-safe, RFDE, and hybrid subclasses;
- select canonical observer, common-action, value-of-information, and obstruction results;
- preserve action/policy and information distinctions.

### Key actions

`V-A001-02`, `B-A001-04`, `B-A001-05`, `B-A002-07`, `B-A002-08`, `B-A002-12`, `X-A001-A002-02`, `X-A001-A002-03`, `V-A002-07`, `V-A002-09`, `V-A002-10`, `V-A002-11`, `V-A006-06`, `V-A006-07`, `V-A006-09`.

### Deliverable

One theorem hierarchy with exact assumptions, finite/infinite horizons, information patterns, and proof status.

